# M44 Execution Changes Log — Avatar Restoration, Green Stomach, Grid & History Data

Autonomous sprint following the strict TDD loop per task: feature contract →
tests → implementation → targeted tests → backlog check-off → git commit,
followed by a full `fvm flutter analyze` and full `fvm flutter test`. Delivered
as per-task commits on `main` (M41–M43 convention). Verification used the
project's pinned FVM SDK (Flutter 3.29.0).

## Task 1: Restore & Harmonize Nutrition Avatar
- `lib/ui/organisms/body_blueprint/body_segment_geometry.dart` — `_torso` now
  renders organic, convex sides using quadratic Bézier curves. Each side bulges
  toward the wider of its two baseline half-widths at mid-height (chest "pecs",
  abdomen "belly") while never exceeding the baseline bounds, so the articulated
  elbow/knee `jointGap` is retained and both tabs share the exact silhouette.
- Bounds and hit tests are unchanged: `body_segment_geometry_test.dart` (twelve
  paths, articulation gap, torso chain, hit tests, anchors) still passes.
- `test/ui/goldens/body_blueprint_painter.png` regenerated for the curved torso.

## Task 2: Protein & Health Green Stomach Semantics
- `lib/core/domain/body_projection/segment_status.dart` — added
  `SegmentStatus.healthy`.
- `lib/ui/organisms/body_blueprint/body_segment_palette.dart` — maps `healthy`
  to `#10B981` (fill at the standard 18% opacity).
- `lib/core/domain/body_projection/segment_balance_calculator.dart` — added
  `isHealthySurplus(input, score)`: the abdomen is healthy only when it is in
  caloric surplus (score above the balanced threshold, `calorieBalance > 0`) and
  protein is at/above target and >= the carb and fat deltas. Carb/fat-led
  surpluses keep warning/critical, and trained muscles are never recoloured.
- Tests: `test/features/m44_task2_green_stomach_test.dart` (palette mapping,
  calculator semantics, diagram-builder integration for healthy vs carb-led
  days).

## Task 3: Blueprint Technical Grid Background
- `lib/ui/organisms/body_blueprint/blueprint_grid_painter.dart` — new painter:
  a fine `cell` lattice, brighter major lines every `majorEvery` (4) cells, and a
  faint centre crosshair; anti-aliasing disabled for crisp technical lines.
- `body_blueprint_diagram.dart` / `unified_body_blueprint.dart` — added
  `showGrid` (default `true`) and render the grid as the first (backmost) layer
  under the figure. Both tabs therefore show it automatically.
- Tests: `test/ui/blueprint_grid_painter_test.dart` (repaint semantics, pixel
  alphas for fine/major/axis lines vs transparent background, widget presence,
  and disabling).

## Task 4: Fix Weekly States & Calendar Data Views
- `lib/core/utils/weekly_stats.dart` — `computeWeeklyStats` now uses the
  persisted `DailyEntry.burned` when recorded, falling back to the flat
  `250 kcal × exercises` estimate only when absent. Previously it always
  recomputed from exercise names, diverging from the post-workout popup and the
  notification check-in.
- `lib/core/state/workout_completion_controller.dart` — optional
  `DailyEntryRepository dailyEntries`. `confirm` upserts today's `DailyEntry`
  with the confirmed exercise names and `summary.caloriesBurned`, preserving any
  nutrition already recorded; `undo` clears the names/burn (also preserving
  nutrition). This is the root cause of the calendar not marking in-app
  workouts.
- `lib/app.dart` — caches a single `DailyEntryRepository` and shares it between
  the calendar, the Weekly Stats view and `WorkoutCompletionController`, so dev
  flavor no longer forks per-call mock stores.
- `lib/core/services/notification_service.dart` — `mealLoggedNotificationBody`
  prefers the persisted burn for consistency.
- Tests: `test/features/m44_task4_weekly_calendar_data_test.dart` (persisted burn
  vs estimate; confirm upserts + preserves nutrition; undo clears; confirmed day
  appears in `getAll()` and feeds `computeWeeklyStats`).

